<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Dr. King asked for a same-day visit before a week of travel. A cold with a sore throat and runny nose began ten days ago; for eight days he has had a cough, worse at night, bringing up some yellow phlegm. He had a low fever for the first two days only. He is not short of breath and has no chest pain apart from aching along his old chest scar when he coughs hard. He has not smoked since the quit date apart from one lapse in June, and he worries that the cough means his lungs are clearing and that he might start again to stop it. He takes sertraline 50 mg and varenicline 1 mg twice daily. He asked whether he needs an antibiotic and whether he can take a cough syrup from the pharmacy. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Cold ten days ago; cough for eight days</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Chest</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Eight days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Cough with some yellow phlegm</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Disturbs his sleep; no breathlessness</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Worse at night</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Eleven weeks off cigarettes; on sertraline and varenicline</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Warm drinks help</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Fever only on the first two days; scar aches with hard coughing</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

