<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute bronchitis (J20.9)</content>. A cough after a cold, with normal pulse, breathing rate, temperature and oxygen saturation and no focal chest signs, fits acute bronchitis rather than pneumonia, so a chest X-ray is not needed under the ACP and CDC advice. Antibiotics do not help acute bronchitis, even with colored phlegm, and the cough may last up to three weeks. Cough syrups containing dextromethorphan should be avoided because, with sertraline, they add a small risk of serotonin toxicity. The scar aching comes from the chest wall with coughing, not the heart. [S]<list><item>No antibiotic.</item><item>Honey in warm drinks, fluids and rest; acetaminophen for the scar aching.</item><item>No dextromethorphan products while he takes sertraline.</item><item>Do not smoke: coughing after quitting is not a reason to restart.</item><item>Return for breathlessness, fever returning, chest pain that is not on coughing, or a cough lasting more than three weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, in early remission (F17.210)</content>. Smoke-free apart from one lapse; continuing varenicline. [S]<list><item>Quitline call this week, before his travel.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder (F32.1)</content>. Mood steady; no suicidal ideation. [S]<list><item>Safety plan unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021); Appropriate Antibiotic Use for Acute Respiratory Tract Infection in Adults: Advice for High-Value Care From the American College of Physicians and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (2016)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Telephone check in one week. Twenty-three-week review as booked. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-15: twenty-three-week review: remission, smoking, blood pressure and lipids. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
